1
00:00:49,010 --> 00:00:52,960
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,350 --> 00:00:56,000
[Episode 14]

3
00:01:00,150 --> 00:01:01,380
It wasn't just

4
00:01:01,970 --> 00:01:03,560
Zhao Changyou who came by just now.

5
00:01:04,510 --> 00:01:06,290
I just vaguely saw

6
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:08,700
what happened that night.

7
00:01:09,430 --> 00:01:10,560
Zhao Changyou

8
00:01:12,150 --> 00:01:13,200
was sitting right there.

9
00:01:14,350 --> 00:01:15,280
There was

10
00:01:16,120 --> 00:01:17,510
a young guy next to him.

11
00:01:18,710 --> 00:01:19,310
Dong.

12
00:01:19,710 --> 00:01:20,539
I'm here.

13
00:01:26,370 --> 00:01:28,000
How'd you get in again?

14
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:30,000
Nobody stopped me downstairs.

15
00:01:38,479 --> 00:01:39,500
What the hell?

16
00:01:40,310 --> 00:01:41,310
It's Li Dewu's.

17
00:01:46,610 --> 00:01:48,400
You really killed Li Dewu?

18
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:49,950
No.

19
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:55,150
Give me the money.

20
00:01:57,830 --> 00:01:58,650
Give me the money.

21
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,220
We agreed on 20,000.

22
00:02:19,310 --> 00:02:20,470
I need a favor, dude.

23
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:22,600
Take it away.

24
00:02:26,579 --> 00:02:27,650
Hurry up.

25
00:02:35,620 --> 00:02:36,600
Take it.

26
00:02:36,620 --> 00:02:37,820
Fine, stop yelling.

27
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,540
Aren't you the boss?

28
00:02:41,470 --> 00:02:42,460
Useless thing.

29
00:02:48,140 --> 00:02:49,670
What kind of person is this?

30
00:02:50,970 --> 00:02:52,200
Ms. Wan,

31
00:02:52,420 --> 00:02:54,140
didn't you say before you left

32
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:57,270
that there were new immortals coming in,

33
00:02:57,370 --> 00:02:59,820
trying to take our turf
and establish themselves,

34
00:02:59,840 --> 00:03:01,610
and even b-burn three sticks of incense?

35
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:03,250
I was wondering,

36
00:03:03,250 --> 00:03:06,180
could you talk to the local immortals

37
00:03:06,180 --> 00:03:07,690
and smooth this over?

38
00:03:10,060 --> 00:03:11,150
Well,

39
00:03:11,150 --> 00:03:12,210
immortals...

40
00:03:13,430 --> 00:03:14,780
Let me put it this way.

41
00:03:14,780 --> 00:03:16,410
If you handle it well,

42
00:03:16,430 --> 00:03:17,390
everyone stays safe.

43
00:03:17,420 --> 00:03:18,710
If you don't,

44
00:03:19,060 --> 00:03:21,410
my life will be on the line,

45
00:03:21,430 --> 00:03:22,390
you know?

46
00:03:22,550 --> 00:03:23,740
Don't be like that.

47
00:03:24,170 --> 00:03:25,790
With your magic power—

48
00:03:25,870 --> 00:03:26,710
How about this?

49
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:29,950
Just tell me how much you need. I'll pay.

50
00:03:30,020 --> 00:03:31,460
Consider it a favor I owe you.

51
00:03:31,940 --> 00:03:33,170
Anything's negotiable.

52
00:03:33,460 --> 00:03:35,110
Just smooth it over for me.

53
00:03:35,140 --> 00:03:36,190
Just name your price.

54
00:03:36,220 --> 00:03:37,200
Stop dawdling.

55
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:18,339
Don't run.

56
00:04:32,409 --> 00:04:34,830
[Fire Sand Pool] [Oil Depot]

57
00:04:39,570 --> 00:04:42,710
[Exit]

58
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:48,950
[Exit]

59
00:06:04,470 --> 00:06:06,090
Page 2565 ten more times.

60
00:06:06,180 --> 00:06:07,980
Tell him to call me back right away.

61
00:06:07,980 --> 00:06:09,070
Ten times.

62
00:06:27,030 --> 00:06:31,950
[Welcome to Tiecheng Petroleum]

63
00:07:01,130 --> 00:07:02,370
I'm done eating.

64
00:07:02,490 --> 00:07:03,410
You take it.

65
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:42,800
Where are they?

66
00:07:43,930 --> 00:07:45,980
My mom had another episode a few days ago.

67
00:07:46,580 --> 00:07:48,460
Hao Peng took her out for a walk

68
00:07:48,909 --> 00:07:50,530
so she won't act up again
in the middle of the night.

69
00:08:08,130 --> 00:08:10,130
How far have you read in that book?

70
00:08:10,690 --> 00:08:12,130
Can that bird fly yet?

71
00:08:13,430 --> 00:08:14,630
It just hit me. You—

72
00:08:15,070 --> 00:08:16,510
You wanna fly too, don't you?

73
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:17,890
But with your condition…

74
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:27,360
Thanks.

75
00:08:33,120 --> 00:08:34,650
That's what the metaphor means, right?

76
00:08:35,100 --> 00:08:35,820
That you wanna...

77
00:08:37,390 --> 00:08:38,080
take off.

78
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,360
Where did that money come from?

79
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:51,820
Don't... Don't be reluctant to spend it.

80
00:08:52,510 --> 00:08:53,250
If you want to fly,

81
00:08:53,250 --> 00:08:54,700
first you gotta eat and get stronger.

82
00:08:55,360 --> 00:08:56,550
Look how skinny you are—

83
00:08:56,890 --> 00:08:58,130
like you've got the strength to fly.

84
00:09:21,820 --> 00:09:23,530
I saved the money.

85
00:09:23,530 --> 00:09:24,320
The bill—

86
00:09:36,460 --> 00:09:38,970
[Savings Bank] [Account Name: Hao Jie]

87
00:09:54,410 --> 00:09:56,510
I was afraid my mom
would have an episode and tear it up,

88
00:09:56,980 --> 00:09:58,200
so I hid it in my underwear.

89
00:09:59,100 --> 00:10:00,340
What do you think I'm trying to do?

90
00:10:01,270 --> 00:10:02,740
Do you think

91
00:10:02,740 --> 00:10:03,770
giving me money

92
00:10:03,770 --> 00:10:05,290
means I'll repay you?

93
00:10:06,690 --> 00:10:08,390
What's this little bit of money good for?

94
00:10:09,150 --> 00:10:10,270
Not even enough for a kidney transplant.

95
00:10:11,030 --> 00:10:13,030
Even for dialysis,
it'll only cover six months.

96
00:10:17,630 --> 00:10:18,890
I know the money isn't enough.

97
00:10:19,960 --> 00:10:21,390
When I first got sick,

98
00:10:22,250 --> 00:10:24,250
plenty of men wanted to help me out

99
00:10:24,270 --> 00:10:25,290
and take advantage of me.

100
00:10:28,930 --> 00:10:30,580
But after a while,

101
00:10:31,120 --> 00:10:32,210
they all ran off.

102
00:10:37,670 --> 00:10:38,910
I didn't mean that.

103
00:10:43,370 --> 00:10:44,750
Then why did you take off your pants?

104
00:10:47,650 --> 00:10:49,360
Maybe it was hot or something.

105
00:10:52,650 --> 00:10:53,250
Isn't this what you want?

106
00:10:53,250 --> 00:10:54,270
No, no, no.

107
00:11:25,790 --> 00:11:27,960
Do you think saving that woman

108
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:30,440
cancels out

109
00:11:30,460 --> 00:11:32,140
everything you've done?

110
00:12:34,070 --> 00:12:35,160
[Tiedong District People's Hospital
Outpatient Payment Notice]

111
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:41,080
[Tiedong District People's Hospital
Outpatient Payment Notice]

112
00:12:44,520 --> 00:12:46,780
[Tiedong District People's Hospital
Outpatient Payment Notice]

113
00:12:50,630 --> 00:12:51,530
What do you mean?

114
00:12:51,530 --> 00:12:52,120
Look.

115
00:12:53,550 --> 00:12:56,680
[Zhao Yongmei] [Sun Li]
[Tiedong District People's Hospital
Cash Receipt]

116
00:12:57,740 --> 00:12:58,460
It's fake.

117
00:12:59,580 --> 00:13:01,180
The first few times I paid,

118
00:13:01,260 --> 00:13:02,320
I saw it.

119
00:13:02,480 --> 00:13:03,530
There are only two cashiers.

120
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:05,460
One is Zhao Yongmei,

121
00:13:05,460 --> 00:13:06,360
and the other is Sun Li.

122
00:13:06,650 --> 00:13:07,650
They work in shifts.

123
00:13:12,390 --> 00:13:13,800
[Zhao Yongmei] [Sun Li]
[Tiedong District People's Hospital
Cash Receipt]

124
00:13:18,420 --> 00:13:19,590
If this gets discovered—

125
00:13:19,620 --> 00:13:21,090
Do you remember

126
00:13:21,390 --> 00:13:22,220
what we said before?

127
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:26,100
To survive,

128
00:13:27,720 --> 00:13:28,960
nothing is off-limits.

129
00:13:37,690 --> 00:13:38,930
[Tiedong District People's Hospital
Outpatient Payment Notice]

130
00:13:47,610 --> 00:13:48,510
If it really gets discovered,

131
00:13:48,510 --> 00:13:49,670
I'll say I did it.

132
00:13:55,430 --> 00:13:59,780
[Water Margin]
[Jonathan Livingston Seagull]

133
00:13:59,870 --> 00:14:07,240
[Pharmacy]

134
00:14:54,650 --> 00:14:55,770
Give it to the dialysis nurse.

135
00:14:55,770 --> 00:14:56,620
Get a blood sugar test first.

136
00:14:56,620 --> 00:14:57,480
Okay, thanks.

137
00:15:11,630 --> 00:15:12,970
Go line up over there.

138
00:15:13,020 --> 00:15:14,230
Okay, thanks.

139
00:15:58,240 --> 00:15:58,870
Hello, ma'am.
